165
00:14:02.273 --> 00:14:06.364
minus refunds. Test four verifies one
exact duplicate and seven

166
00:14:06.364 --> 00:14:10.455
rejected boundary rows. Test five verifies
two accepted rows and

167
00:14:10.455 --> 00:14:14.545
gross 100 in that boundary fixture. Test
six confirms a

168
00:14:14.545 --> 00:14:18.636
baseline refund with an empty reference is
accepted, with refunds

169
00:14:18.636 --> 00:14:22.727
25 and net 75. Together these six tests
cover duplicates,

170
00:14:22.727 --> 00:14:26.818
conflicts, missing identifiers, zero,
negative, signed, decimal, noninteger

171
00:14:26.818 --> 00:14:30.909
amounts, unknown kinds, reconciliation,
exact output order, and valid-schema

172
00:14:30.909 --> 00:14:35.000
process success independently.

173
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:39.308
The six baseline tests launch
